==English==

===Etymology===
First coined to serve as an {{l/en|antonym}} of {{term|entropy|lang=en}}, substituting its {{term||en-|lang=en}} element (representing the prepositional prefix {{term|ἐν|lang=grc}}, ''en'', “in” in its {{etyl|grc|en}} etymon {{term|ἐντροπία|lang=grc}}, ''entropia'', “a turning towards”) with {{term||ex-|lang=en}} (representing the {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|ἐξ|lang=grc}}, ''ex'', “out of”, “from”); because {{term||ἐξ|tr=ex|lang=grc}} takes the form {{term|ἐκ|tr=ek|lang=grc}} when prefixed to an element beginning with {{term|τ|tr=t|lang=grc}}, the analogical spelling is {{term|ectropy|lang=en}} (or, alternatively, {{term|ektropy|lang=en}}), as if after the {{etyl|grc|en}} *{{term||ἐκτροπία|tr=ektropia|a turning out of|lang=grc}}.

===Noun===
{{head|en|noun}}

# a [[concept]] that [[life]] will [[continue]] to [[expand]] [[throughout]] the [[universe]] as a [[result]] of [[human]] [[intelligence]] and [[technology]]

